  "result": "Reservations with expiry are in, and `npm test` passes (175 tests, 0 failed). That includes 10 new tests I added to `test/store.test.js` and `test/api.test.js`.\n\n- **Store (`src/store.js`):** I added `reserve`, `confirm`, `release` and `getAvailable`. `removeItem` now checks available stock instead of physical stock. Time comes only from the store's `clock`. A reservation counts as expired once `clock() >= creation time + ttlMs`.\n- **API (`src/api.js`):** `GET /stock/:sku` now also returns `available`. I added `POST /reservations`, `POST /reservations/:id/confirm` and `DELETE /reservations/:id` with the status codes you specified.\n\nA few behaviours your spec didn't cover:\n- Expired reservations stay in memory, so confirming one returns `RESERVATION_EXPIRED` rather than `RESERVATION_NOT_FOUND`. They are never cleaned up, so memory grows with every reservation that expires without being confirmed or released.\n- `ttlMs` isn't validated.\n- `POST /reservations` returns 400 for any error other than `INSUFFICIENT_STOCK`.\n- `POST /reservations/:id/confirm` returns 404 for any error other than `RESERVATION_EXPIRED`.",
